id: pm-ts-starter-dcep
title: Propagate the docstring gate entry guard fix
description: "The isMainInvocation entry guard swallowed realpathSync ENOENT and returned false, causing npm run docstring to exit 0 having scanned nothing — a mandatory release gate reporting success without doing its job. Propagate the throw instead so a broken environment fails loudly."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[2]: docstrings,gate
created_at: "2026-08-10T05:48:43.865Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T19:13:01.765Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-21T19:12:54.664Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-21T19:12:54.664Z"
author: pi-agent
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T19:11:22.582Z",codex-agent,"Authorized tracker reconciliation, audit 2026-10-21. Owner-authorized takeover of any historical assignment for this verified terminal transition. Reverified current main e5d15d4964cc: merged #58 (b1eeac5); docstring entrypoint guard and its delivery retained; source tree exactly matches the audited snapshot. **Propagate the docstring gate entry guard fix.** [PR #58](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ts-starter/pull/58) propagates docstring guard realpath failures and includes the executable-entry negative control."
notes[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-10T05:48:47.698Z",pi-agent,"Defect: isMainInvocation caught realpathSync ENOENT and returned false, so the top-level selector called the no-op placeholder instead of main. npm run docstring exited 0 having scanned nothing — a mandatory release check reporting success without doing its job."
  "2026-08-10T05:48:48.657Z",pi-agent,"Fix: removed the try/catch so realpathSync propagates. An unresolvable argv[1] means the environment is broken after Node already loaded this file, and a broken environment must not silently satisfy a gate. The JSDoc now documents @throws and corrects the inverted fails-closed language."
  "2026-08-10T05:48:49.186Z",pi-agent,"Verification: npm test passes (143 tests), npm run docstring exits 0 (4 files, 18 declarations), npm run coverage meets thresholds (100%), and node --experimental-strip-types confirms isMainInvocation throws ENOENT on an unresolvable argv[1] instead of returning false."
  "2026-08-10T06:44:22.363Z",pi-agent,"Greptile (P2 on pm-beads) and CodeRabbit (Major on pm-slack) independently flagged the one-sided comparison in isMainInvocation: pathToFileURL(realpathSync(entry)).href === moduleUrl resolves only argv[1], leaving moduleUrl holding the symlink under --preserve-symlinks. Canonicalising both sides through realpathSync fixes it. Verified by measurement: with moduleUrl holding the symlink path, both-sides (new) returns true while one-sided (old) returns false."
  "2026-08-10T07:21:19.066Z",pi-agent,"The previous symlink test (isMainInvocation resolves a symlinked entry path to the real module URL) passed argv[1] as the link and moduleUrl as the REAL path, which the old one-sided comparison pathToFileURL(realpathSync(entry)).href === moduleUrl also satisfied — it could not distinguish the fixed implementation from the broken one. Added a new test (canonicalizes a symlinked moduleUrl, as --preserve-symlinks produces) that puts the symlink in moduleUrl (pathToFileURL(link).href), which is what Node records in import.meta.url under --preserve-symlinks. Verified by measurement: reverting to the old one-sided comparison makes the new test fail (fail 1), restoring the canonicalization makes it pass (fail 0). The existing symlink test is retained because argv[1] arriving through an npm bin shim is a separate real case."
close_reason: "Reverified current main e5d15d4964cc: merged #58 (b1eeac5); docstring entrypoint guard and its delivery retained; source tree exactly matches the audited snapshot. **Propagate the docstring gate entry guard fix.** [PR #58](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ts-starter/pull/58) propagates docstring guard realpath failures and includes the executable-entry negative control."
body: ""
